        "title": "fix(ios): remove debug icon outer rim",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where the new iOS and Watch debug app icon showed a white rim outside its yellow-and-black construction border.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe construction treatment now runs full-bleed to the canvas edge while preserving the approved lobster, center panel, and debug badge. All iPhone, iPad, Watch, and marketing sizes were regenerated from the corrected 1024 px master.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDebug builds remain easy to distinguish, without an unintended white outline after the system applies its app-icon mask.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Validated all 42 manifest-referenced PNG assets are present, opaque, and match their declared dimensions.\n- Verified all four 1024 px master corners are construction-stripe colors rather than white.\n- Inspected the 1024 px master plus 180 px, 40 px, and Watch marketing outputs.\n- `git diff --check`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local ...` — clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
